# CATEGORY: recurrence-loops / unsafe output-feedback exemplar
# CLAIM: this shape is intentionally NOT runtime-gate safe.
#
# It demonstrates the cardinality hazard found in output-feedback recurrence:
# the expression runs on both Tau binaries, but some traces emit a shortened or
# extended output stream. That means a runtime host cannot safely align verdicts
# with input transitions.
#
# Keep this file as negative evidence. Do not promote it into recommended/.
set charvar off

always
  (o1[t]:sbf = (o1[t-1]:sbf | i1[t]:sbf)).
end
